Build artefacts under `build/` (including `printf-toto.exe` / `test_core.exe` on Windows) are gitignored. Directories stay in the repo via `build/.gitkeep` and `build/tests/.gitkeep`.

## Building on Linux

```sh
make clean && make && make test
./build/printf-toto --version
```

## Building on Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64)

**Recommended:** open **MSYS2 UCRT64** from the Start menu:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/printf-toto
make clean && make && make test
./build/printf-toto --version
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`build/printf-toto` or `build/printf-toto.exe`). Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, and CMD.

### Git Bash caveat

Git Bash can build if **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is early on `PATH`**. Otherwise `gcc --version` may work while `cc1` fails silently (DLL load order). Prefer UCRT64 shell or:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- Pure helpers declared in headers (or isolated `.c` units) are what tests exercise.
- Prefer tests that do **not** link the full CLI; avoid pulling `main` into `test_core`.
- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c`.
- Debug binary is linked in one step from sources with `CFLAGS_DEBUG` (does not reuse release `.o` files).
